COVID-19 Data Analysis Project Summary
Project Title

COVID-19 Data Analysis Using Python

Summary

This project analyzes the global COVID-19 pandemic using real-world data from the Our World in Data dataset. 
The aim is to understand how COVID-19 spread over time by examining daily cases, total cases, deaths, 
and vaccination trends, with a primary focus on India and comparisons with other countries. 
GitHub
+1

Using Python, Pandas, Matplotlib, and Seaborn in Google Colab, the data is cleaned, processed, and visualized through charts. 
The project demonstrates basic data science techniques such as data collection, data cleaning, exploratory data analysis (EDA), and data visualization.


  
Objectives

Analyze COVID-19 cases and deaths in India.

Compare total cases across major countries.

Visualize daily and cumulative trends.

Study vaccination progress using real data.

Generate meaningful insights from the dataset.




  
